  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Codex Native for DSH",
      "text": "Use your ChatGPT account to work with Codex models inside DeepSeek Harness. Chat, share images, use tools and skills, and continue longer tasks without leaving DSH.\n\n[简体中文](README.zh.md) · [What's new in 0.2.3](RELEASE_NOTES.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "What you can do",
      "text": "- **Sign in and choose a model:** use your ChatGPT account, refresh the models available to it, and choose a model and thinking effort. New model choices and runtime updates are picked up when needed, without a separate manual update routine.\n- **Chat and work with images:** send text and images, use DSH tools, and continue conversations with their earlier tool results and image attachments, including after a restart.\n- **Carry out local tasks with permission:** connect Codex command and file-operation requests to DSH approval prompts. Approve an offered action once or reject it; the plugin does not silently grant lasting permission. Available actions still depend on your installed tools and sandbox settings.\n- **Answer questions in the conversation:** select an option or enter your own answer. Your answer is sent back to the task and shown in chat without another send step.\n- **Find and use skills:** search skills from local files and connected plugins, then read the instructions needed for the task. Choose DSH-managed discovery or the native skill catalog, and optionally set a skill-context budget.\n- **Manage longer conversations:** use context compaction and overflow recovery, r"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install or update",
      "text": "Current version: **0.2.3**. The fixed tag and installation package include runtime files; no build is needed.\n\n**First installation (Desktop):** Open **Plugins → Add plugin** in the sidebar (or **Install a third-party plugin** in the arrow menu). Paste the complete line below into **Package name or address**, click **Install**, check the version and click **Enable now**.\n\n```text\ngithub:Tests4gptplay/dsh-codex-native#v0.2.3\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install or update",
      "text": "**Updating:** Use the same dialog with the new versioned source above, verify the installed version and enable it. Retain existing settings and user files. If DSH reports that it is already installed or requires removal first, follow that message to remove only the plugin entry and install the new version; do not clear DSH data or manually delete plugin directories. Restart only when DSH asks you to; fully quit and reopen it, including the Desktop tray process."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install or update",
      "text": "After enabling, sign in through the plugin settings if needed and select a model in DSH. Updating does not require clearing account storage.\n\n**Alternative package:** Paste this `.tgz` URL into the same **Package name or address** field, or download it and enter its full absolute path. No extraction is needed. The path must be on the computer running DSH.\n\n```text\nhttps://github.com/Tests4gptplay/dsh-codex-native/releases/download/v0.2.3/dsh-codex-native-0.2.3.tgz\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install or update",
      "text": "**Web:** Run this on the computer hosting the service. Stop the corresponding Web profile before updating and restart it after success. Web and Desktop installations are separate.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add 'github:Tests4gptplay/dsh-codex-native#v0.2.3'\n```\n\nAlternatively, replace the source in the command with the `.tgz` URL above or the downloaded file's absolute path."
    },
    {
      "section": "Important limits",
      "text": "Approval prompts do not bypass the sandbox. Windows helper maintenance is Windows-only and supports a specific known helper version; read its guidance before applying a repair. Linux and macOS runtime selection is included, but this release does not claim new macOS live testing. See the [release notes](RELEASE_NOTES.md) for the verified scope and remaining test boundaries."
    },
    {
      "section": "More information",
      "text": "[Detailed setup](https://github.com/Tests4gptplay/dsh-codex-native/blob/main/docs/INSTALL.md) · [Configuration and engineering records](https://github.com/Tests4gptplay/dsh-codex-native/tree/main/docs) · [Source and issue reports](https://github.com/Tests4gptplay/dsh-codex-native)"
    },
    {
      "section": "More information",
      "text": "Community integration; DeepSeek Harness is developed by DeepSeek and Codex by OpenAI. Original project and artwork attribution are retained in [LICENSE](LICENSE), [project credits](https://github.com/Tests4gptplay/dsh-codex-native/blob/72b092f364c913722e2013de43878d22b35fc741/README.md#license-and-attribution), and the bundled Lobe Icons license. Reference-period dates use codex-reset.com announcements."
    },
    {
